WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.037
"Blocking the Cancer Metastasis Enzyme
MMP-9 with Beans and Chickpeas"

00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:12.857
Although we’re spending
billions of dollars

00:00:12.857 --> 00:00:15.000
on fancy new types of chemotherapy,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.400
the overflowing sink that is
cancer treatment is expected

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.520
to rise by about 70 percent
over the next two decades

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.960
because drugs are being used
to merely mop up the mess

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.360
rather than turn off the faucet.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.760
You can’t really give drugs
to people to prevent cancer

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.720
because of the side effects and
cost, but there is said to be

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.160
overwhelming evidence that
the dietary bioactive compounds

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.040
found in whole plant-based
foods have signiﬁcant

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.160
anticancer and cancer
preventive properties.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.640
In a previous video, I talked
about the impact of diet

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.000
and nutrition on the
ten hallmarks of cancer.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.880
The bottom line is that evidence
points to a diet with minimal

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.600
animal products, and perhaps more
importantly, maximal plant foods.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.640
Some foods that appear to be
particularly beneficial include fruit

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.320
(especially berries), a variety
of vegetables (especially greens),

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.120
legumes (which are beans, split
peas, chickpeas, and lentils),

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.360
nuts and seeds (especially
flaxseeds), mushrooms, onions,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.080
garlic, herbs and spices
(for example, turmeric),

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.840
and, as a beverage, green tea.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.840
Chemotherapy may
not even be particularly

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.600
good at mopping up the mess.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.880
Cancer drugs often impair
quality of life and fail to extend

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.280
patient survival.
Let me say that again.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.200
You’re paying for drugs, maybe
selling your house to pay for drugs,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:37.520
that may just be making
your life worse for no benefit.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.650
Some have suggested we demand
at least three months of extended

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:43.120
life from pharmaceuticals,
but if we demand

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.200
that chemo actually works,
might they give up altogether?

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.920
On the other hand, maybe by
mandating clinically important

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.760
benefits—what a concept—
maybe big pharma would reallocate

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.520
resources towards targeting
the more critical cancer processes

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.520
like metastatic spread,
because it’s the tumor metastasis

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.320
that accounts for 90 percent
of cancer-related deaths.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.040
Who cares if some drug
shrinks your primary tumor if

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.240
it’s spreading and cutting
your life just as short?

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.280
What about controlling metastatic
cancer with some of those

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.560
natural bioactive
compounds in plants?

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.280
Evidently it has been proven that
plant phytochemicals are able

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.600
to inhibit nearly every step of the
invasion through metastasis cascade,

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.320
at least in vitro, in a petri dish.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.554
Here’s a list of some
purported dietary sources of

00:02:29.554 --> 00:02:32.720
antimetastatic phytochemicals,
all shown to block all sorts of

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.640
cancer signaling pathways,
but let me focus on one:

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.520
matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs).

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.320
Since about 90 percent of cancer
disability and death is due

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:47.200
to cancer spreading, metastasis,
let’s talk about these MMPs

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:51.600
which actively participate
in the whole metastatic journey.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.560
Matrix metalloproteinases are
enzymes that allow the cancer

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.240
to tunnel through the
surrounding flesh and invade the

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.240
lymph or blood vessels
and then enable it

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.280
to burrow in and grow
somewhere else.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.840
So, Big Pharma developed matrix
metalloproteinase inhibitor drugs,

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.920
which worked great in animal
models but caused severe

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.800
side effects when
they tried them on humans.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.400
So, what about using food?

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.200
There are special proteins in
legumes that reduce MMP activity.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.600
What else might you
expect from a Dr. Lima?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.920
But which is the leading legume?

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.960
Researchers tested eight
different kinds: lupin beans,

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.480
chickpeas, split peas,
black-eyed peas, lentils, and

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.280
more common beans (like
kidney, black, or pinto),

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:44.080
fava beans, and soybeans.
Which do you think worked best?

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.840
Without any beans, the matrix
metalloproteinase activity

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.600
churned away at around 100 percent
and dripping on some protein

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.320
from pea soup-type peas
didn’t seem to help much,

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:58.240
but the black-eyed peas, lentils,
common beans, and fava beans

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:01.453
cut enzyme activity by
more than 50 percent.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.600
Guess what slashed activity
by more than 90 percent?

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.280
Lupin beans, chickpeas, and soybeans.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:13.760
Yeah, but does this translate into
slowing down the cancer’s spread?

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.960
Researchers plated a layer
of human colon cancer cells

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.920
in a petri dish and then
took a razor blade to clear

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.919
a strip down the middle.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:26.080
Within 48 hours, the cancer
quickly converged to fill the gap.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:28.640
But when a little protein
from lupin beans, chickpeas,

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:32.160
or soybeans was dripped on,
it looks like the cancer cells

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.200
struggled to close the distance.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.600
Okay, but they used raw beans.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.000
You don’t know if these anti-
cancer proteins are destroyed

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.120
by cooking until you put it to the test.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.960
And the matrix metalloproteinase
inhibitors in soybeans at least,

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:50.058
remain active after cooking.

00:04:50.058 --> 00:04:53.040
So, maybe it’s no wonder that
dietary legume consumption

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.280
reduces risk of colorectal
cancer. Yeah, but colon cancer,

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.600
which sprouts from the
inner lining of the colon,

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.720
could potentially come in contact
with some of these bean proteins.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.760
Presumably they wouldn’t
get into the bloodstream.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.720
Those eating vegetarian do
seem to have significantly

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.920
lower levels of matrix
metalloproteinases, but this is just

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.960
thought to be due to their
lower levels of inflammation,

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:19.120
similar to the way non-smokers
also have lower MMP levels.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:22.160
This is good, because this
enzyme isn’t just a cancer biomarker,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.400
but also may be involved
in autoimmune diseases

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.560
and cardiovascular disease.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.600
The machete-type nature of
this enzyme can hack through

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.720
the inflamed cholesterol-filled
atherosclerotic lesions

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:36.880
lining diseased arteries and
cause the plaque to rupture.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.200
People know that those eating
more plant-based tend to have

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.600
less heart disease but
may not realize they harbor

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.240
significantly less cancer risk too,

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.768
particularly among those eating
strictly plant-based diets.

